  "title": "Apps & Integrations | Picflow",
  "content": "Picflow Mobile\nShare galleries and review feedback on the go with the Picflow mobile app for Apple iOS and Android.\nConnect the tools you already use. Publish from Lightroom and Capture One, keep assets moving through Dropbox or Google Drive, and automate any creative workflow with Zapier.\nNew\nDrag folders straight from Finder into Picflow. Large uploads run in the background while you keep working.\nPublish galleries directly from Lightroom Classic and sync new edits to Picflow with a single click.\nUpload directly from Capture One and stream shoots in real-time without interrupting your tethered workflow.\nSave images to a Picflow gallery while browsing the web. Collect references and inspiration without breaking flow.\nConnect Picflow to thousands of apps. Trigger workflows when galleries are created, shared, or approved.\nImport files from Dropbox straight into your galleries without any downloading and re-uploading in between.\nPull assets from Google Drive into Picflow and keep client deliveries organized in one place.\nImport files from Box into your galleries and connect enterprise storage to your review workflow.\nAdd your Tag Manager container to galleries and run your own tracking, pixels, and remarketing tags.\nConnect Google Analytics to your galleries and measure visits, views, and engagement with your own property.\nZapier\nGet notified in Slack when clients view, comment on, or approve a gallery. No more inbox digging.\nTurn gallery approvals and comments into Asana tasks so production never loses track of feedback.\nSoon\nPlace approved assets from Picflow directly into your Figma files and keep design work in sync.\nUse approved images from your galleries directly in Canva designs. No manual exports needed.\nWe have more integrations planned. Is there one you wish we had? Let us know",
